<decision #track.simplify_codument_actions.defaults apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = false confidence = 0.99 reversibility = "moderate" } (
  <question ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPR>
  What should planning create by default and when should attractor checks run?
  </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPR>
  <recommendation ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPS>
  Always create design.md and decisions.xnl; keep durable folders on demand and make fresh attractor checks explicit or high-risk final-phase only.
  </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPS>
  <answer {  } (
    <raw-answer ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPT>
    The user confirmed these defaults and requested lower attractor frequency without splitting the coding profile.
    </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPT>
    <decision-text ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPV>
    Planning creates design.md and decisions.xnl unconditionally, while decisions/ and memory/ are demand-created. Ordinary actions and phases do not run fresh attractor checks by default.
    </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPV>
    <rationale ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPW>
    This preserves durable planning context while avoiding repeated full-context review work.
    </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPW>
    <evidence ?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPX>
    Mission decisions action_taxonomy, maintain_track, and attractor.
    </?01M02EGVBE4FPMA727YKFJ9YPX>
  )>
)>
